Subject: [PATCH 3/5] =?UTF-8?q?task=20#931=20(2/3)=20=E2=80=94=20klein4=5F?=
 =?UTF-8?q?random(D,=20default=5Frng(N))=20->=20klein4=5Fexpand(D,=20N):?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=2011=20sites,=20numbers=20CHANGE?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Still the DRAWN regime, but this group is NOT a rename and its numbers move.

Every one of these 11 sites built a FRESH numpy generator inline and consumed
only its first draw — default_rng(i*31), default_rng(seed+1000+r),
default_rng(77) — so the site was already a deterministic mint wearing a
stochastic signature. klein4_expand is the honest spelling of that.

What changes: the underlying stream. numpy PCG64 -> stdlib MT19937, so the
vector VALUES differ. What does not change: the keying. Distinct seeds still
give distinct vectors, and neighbouring keys (i*31 vs i*31+1, seed+3000+2r vs
+2r+1) stay distinct, so anything these scripts measure over a population of
mutually-unrelated random atoms — capacity, discrimination, crosstalk — is
statistically equivalent at different exact values.

No number here was chosen to be preserved; the regime was chosen and the number
followed.

Side effect worth naming: each of these 11 sites was a numpy call, and none of
them is now. docs/srmech/no-numpy.constraints.txt pins numpy==0 precisely so
numpy cannot enter a srmech venv, yet 321 files in this research tree import it.
This is 11 fewer.

